Wrong (A): Section 7872 specifically treats the interest differential on below-market family loans as a gift, regardless of the familial relationship; being family members does not create an exemption.
Wrong (B): The principal is a loan obligation, not a gift; only the below-market interest element ($22,500 annually) is treated as a gift under Section 7872.
